   132	## Session 2 — structural investigation (deeper pass). Six rigorous dead-end proofs.
   133
   134	**1. Sign non-recomputability (THEOREM, kills tape fusion).** The walk recurrence is
   135	`t ← (t + (−1)^sign·s)/2` with both operands odd and `sign = t1⊕s1` (sign=0→add iff
   136	t1=s1; this exactly makes the halved result odd, preserving the invariant). Mod-4 check
   137	of both candidate pre-images: t⁺=2t'−s always has t⁺1=s1 (consistent with sign=0) and
   138	t⁻=2t'+s always has t⁻1≠s1 (consistent with sign=1). Both pre-images are always valid ⇒
   139	the sign bit is information-theoretically lost from the value state ⇒ the tape cannot be
   140	freed early or recomputed. Tape=703 is NECESSARY for this recurrence.
   141
   142	**2. Pebbling loses to the plateau.** Checkpointing (u,v) at round B costs 2·width(B)
   143	qubits to free B tape bits; the schedule keeps 2·width(r)+r nearly balanced against any
   144	cut point, and the uncompute re-walks cost ≈ +29% T for −3% Q at the best single split.
   145	Always net-negative.
